WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.676 --> 00:00:11.590
Hi, I am Danielle Oberdier,
the founder of DiKayoData.com,

00:00:11.590 --> 00:00:15.730
data science media company,
and the Data Femme Podcast.

00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:18.640
And I'm here to talk to
you about how content

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:24.500
makes our industry go round and
stay connected to one another.

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:27.670
So if you have more questions
because this is a lightning

00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:31.090
talk, please reach out
on Twitter @dikayodata,

00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:33.760
or at my site, DiKayoData.com.

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:37.750
I'm always happy to talk
and clarify more things

00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:39.040
that I don't get to this time.

00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:44.270
So what to make?

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:45.850
There are several
types of content

00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:49.960
that you can make when you're
starting out making content.

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:52.510
One, obviously, is
an audio podcast

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:56.470
but that takes a ton of time
editing, finding guests,

00:00:56.470 --> 00:00:59.080
finding sponsors, and
it's a lot of work,

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:02.920
whereas a blog is only
the amount of work

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:04.180
that you want to make it.

00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:07.930
You can be amazing like Julia
Silge and do YouTube tutorials,

00:01:07.930 --> 00:01:10.570
but that is not something
within my expertise.

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:11.530
I do blog.

00:01:11.530 --> 00:01:12.310
I love it.

00:01:12.310 --> 00:01:15.490
I love making tutorials
that people can just

00:01:15.490 --> 00:01:18.640
look at really quickly without
turning off their TV shows

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:20.200
and just get right to the point.

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:23.560
I love writing about
general trends,

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:26.500
career trends in the industry.

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:30.460
What's interesting is that
long form content is totally

00:01:30.460 --> 00:01:35.210
in average of 1,200 words,
is what is the most popular.

00:01:35.210 --> 00:01:38.840
So if you want to just
write content every month,

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:41.200
every two months, and you
have something to say,

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:43.960
know that that long form
piece is going to be something

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:46.880
that people are interested in.

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:48.940
In terms of where
to share it, that's

00:01:48.940 --> 00:01:52.240
where I just want to give a
shout out to email marketing.

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:54.430
Email marketing
is very important.

00:01:54.430 --> 00:01:59.380
Nine out of 10 marketers
still use email

00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:04.660
to promote their products,
and 81% of small businesses

00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:07.450
use email as the primary
way of connecting

00:02:07.450 --> 00:02:08.690
with their customers.

00:02:08.690 --> 00:02:10.750
So I do have an email list.

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:13.270
I suggest that if you have
a product that you really

00:02:13.270 --> 00:02:15.520
want to circulate
to your audience,

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:17.770
definitely set up an email.

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:22.090
There are so many ways to set
up an email list with your blog.

00:02:22.090 --> 00:02:24.250
I recommend Squarespace,
and I am always

00:02:24.250 --> 00:02:27.920
available to talk about
this, like I said.

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:29.450
Who it helps.

00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:32.150
Obviously, having
content in our industry

00:02:32.150 --> 00:02:35.810
really helps bring new
talent into the fold.

00:02:35.810 --> 00:02:39.470
You can't just expect
to post on LinkedIn

00:02:39.470 --> 00:02:43.130
and have all the right
people get to your message.

00:02:43.130 --> 00:02:45.860
You do have to write content
that is targeted towards people

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:49.400
that might not feel comfortable
addressing certain issues

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:56.600
in the industry, talk to them,
bring them in, definitely think

00:02:56.600 --> 00:02:58.910
about what kind of
content you're addressing,

00:02:58.910 --> 00:03:06.170
think about current events, and
it obviously helps newcomers.

00:03:06.170 --> 00:03:09.440
It also helps all
of us who might not

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:10.730
be newcomers to the field.

00:03:10.730 --> 00:03:11.660
Why it matters.

00:03:11.660 --> 00:03:14.420
Well, a lot of us don't
think about talking

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:17.000
more about content
after our work is

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:19.010
over with just the few
packages that we've

00:03:19.010 --> 00:03:24.230
been working with all day
that our projects tend to use.

00:03:24.230 --> 00:03:27.710
If we want to think outside the
box and relate to each other,

00:03:27.710 --> 00:03:30.230
then the content that
we circulate really

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:33.180
fosters that discussion
outside of the workplace.

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:38.450
And I think it gives those of
us that are in higher positions

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:40.370
a way to connect
with other people

00:03:40.370 --> 00:03:43.280
in other industries who are
doing really good things

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:44.450
that they didn't know about.

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:46.970
I know that Data Femme is
often a connector for people

00:03:46.970 --> 00:03:50.240
who never would have met but
listen to the same podcast

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:52.460
and then end up having
a discussion maybe

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:53.315
on social media.

00:03:55.930 --> 00:03:59.430
And here, we finally
get to how to succeed.

00:03:59.430 --> 00:04:02.100
Consistency is really
important but you

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:03.600
can set the barometer for that.

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:07.500
You do not have to say that
consistency means every day.

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:09.310
It could mean once a month.

00:04:09.310 --> 00:04:13.020
It could even mean once a
year for certain projects.

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:15.270
Really, what matters
is that you're

00:04:15.270 --> 00:04:17.880
consistent about how you
promote your content.

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:20.640
You're consistent in having
discussions in person, at work,

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:21.930
on social media.

00:04:21.930 --> 00:04:26.370
That really matters because that
is really the most important

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:30.750
of your content's life story,
is who it reaches and how.

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:33.450
So you can make the best
content in the world

00:04:33.450 --> 00:04:35.640
but if it never
reaches anybody, you're

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:38.370
not going to really
succeed in the way

00:04:38.370 --> 00:04:42.430
that the industry
could benefit from.

00:04:42.430 --> 00:04:48.840
So definitely, no matter how
much you write or record,

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:51.750
make sure that you're
always having conversations

00:04:51.750 --> 00:04:56.130
to help you grow, your content
grow, and the industry grow.

00:04:56.130 --> 00:04:58.310
Thank you so much.

